From 20260813-susfs-uname Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:43:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] susfs: hook spoof_uname into Pulsar uname implementation

The Pulsar 4.19 base already has its own uname spoofing logic. SuSFS
provides the hook through susfs.h, so include the header and call the
hook from the existing implementation.

Signed-off-by: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
---
 kernel/sys.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sys.c b/kernel/sys.c
--- a/kernel/sys.c
+++ b/kernel/sys.c
@@ -35,5 +35,6 @@
 #include <linux/nospec.h>
 
 #include <linux/kmsg_dump.h>
+#include <linux/susfs.h>
 /* Move somewhere else to avoid recompiling? */
 #include <generated/utsrelease.h>
@@ -1247,4 +1248,7 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE1(newuname, struct new_utsname __user *, name)
 
 	down_read(&uts_sem);
 	memcpy(&tmp, utsname(), sizeof(tmp));
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_UNAME
+	susfs_spoof_uname(&tmp);
+#endif
 	if (cur_uid == 0 &&
